# Cloudflare Pages serves 404.html for any path that isn't a real static
# file — Vite's build only emits index.html at the root, so /practice,
# /daily, /rush, /browse, /legal all 404 on a cold/direct load without
# this. Each real route is rewritten (200, not a redirect — the URL stays
# as typed) to index.html so the SPA can boot and its own router takes it
# from there.
#
# No wildcard (`/* /index.html 200`) on purpose: that would make every URL
# on the domain return 200 with the app shell, which is both bad for
# crawlers and breaks the "an unknown path returns a real 404" requirement.
# Anything not listed below keeps falling through to 404.html.
/practice /index.html 200
/daily /index.html 200
/rush /index.html 200
/browse /index.html 200
/legal /index.html 200
